# Phase F — build-context trim for the console-backend image.
# The build context is the monorepo root, so without this every build
# ships node_modules, .git, the renderer out/, previews, and docs over
# the wire before a single layer runs.
#
# Deliberately conservative: only large directories the Dockerfile never
# COPYs are excluded. Blanket *.txt/*.json excludes are avoided so the
# console-backend build artifacts (ipc-channels.txt, generated-*.json)
# stay in the context.

# Git history
.git
**/.git/**

# Dependencies (the Dockerfile runs `npm ci` itself)
node_modules
**/node_modules/**

# Build outputs (the renderer is rebuilt inside the image)
agent-desktop/out
agent-desktop/dist
**/out/
**/dist/
agent-desktop/previews

# Docs + external reference repos (large, never built into the image)
docs
agent-desktop/docs

# Local scratch / editor state
*.log
.vscode
.idea
**/.DS_Store
